# ABSTRACT

The Student Grievance Redressal Portal is a web-based application designed to provide students with a simple, accessible and transparent platform for submitting and tracking their grievances within an educational institution.
In many colleges, complaints are often communicated through paper forms, verbal requests or scattered emails, making it difficult for students to monitor their complaints and for administrators to manage them efficiently.

The proposed portal provides a centralized system where students can register, log in, submit grievances and track the status of their complaints. 
Faculty members or administrators can access a dashboard to review submitted grievances, update their status and record the actions taken towards resolution.
Additionally, students can provide feedback once their grievances have been resolved, helping improve the grievance-handling process.

The application is developed using HTML, CSS and JavaScript, with LocalStorage used for storing and managing data within the browser.
The portal aims to improve communication between students and college administration, promote transparency, reduce delays in grievance handling and provide a more organized approach to addressing student concerns.
